    <h1>Terms of use and disclaimer</h1>
    <p>By using honestpenny.ca you agree to these terms. They're written to be read, so please do.</p>

    <h2>General information, not advice</h2>
    <p>Everything on Honest Penny, including guides, calculators and emails, is <strong>general information</strong> for people in Alberta and Canada. It is not financial, investment, tax, legal or insurance advice, and it isn't tailored to you. We are not registered or licensed to give personal advice about securities, insurance, mortgages, tax or law. Before you make a decision, think about your own situation and, if you need to, get advice from a qualified professional. Free non-profit options include credit counsellors and volunteer tax clinics.</p>

    <h2>Accuracy</h2>
    <p>We work hard to get things right: we use official sources, show the date we last checked each fact, and fix mistakes when we find them. But rules, rates and deadlines change, sometimes without notice, and we can make mistakes. <strong>Always confirm with the official source</strong> (we link to it) before you act, especially for deadlines, amounts and eligibility.</p>

    <h2>Calculators</h2>
    <p>Calculators give estimates based on the numbers you enter and the assumptions we explain under each one. They aren't quotes or guarantees, and real results will differ.</p>

    <h2>Other websites</h2>
